OL,3,GNEWSAResidents are 'sick to death' of
OL,4,Anoisy driving
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents calling for action against
OL,7,Fdangerous and loud driving have
OL,8,Fdescribed how their towns are being
OL,9,Fused as "racetracks".
OL,11,FElaine Kent from Lee-on-the-Solent,
OL,12,FHampshire, said the sound of speeding
OL,13,Fvehicles and "popping" exhausts are a
OL,14,Fnightly occurrence in her area, often
OL,15,Fgoing on until the early hours of the
OL,16,Fmorning.
OL,18,FShe said "everyone is sick to death of
OL,19,Fit" and "something has to be done
OL,20,Fbecause I believe somebody will get
OL,21,Fkilled soon, it's very, very
OL,22,Fdangerous".
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
